<title>FRANCE: Air France Jan-June 97 cargo tonnage share at ADP.</title>
<headline>Air France Jan-June 97 cargo tonnage share at ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France 's share of global air cargo tonnage handled at the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in the first six months of 1997 was stable compared to 1996 as a whole, Aeroport de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Air France's share of ADP's global cargo tonnage in the period in question, totalling 552,149 tonnes, was 55.6 percent compared to 55.5 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>The top 10 cargo-handling airlines at the ADP, by tonnage share, in January-June 1997, together with 1996 full-year tonnage share, were as follows:</p>
<p>		    Jan-June 1997  1996 (full year)</p>
<p>			percent	percent</p>
<p>Air France	  55.6	    55.5</p>
<p>Federal Express    7.8	     6.8</p>
<p>Air France Europe  2.6	     3.8</p>
<p>(ex-Air Inter)</p>
<p>American Airlines  2.2	     2.0</p>
<p>Air Canada	   2.2	     1.7</p>
<p>L'Aeropostale	1.8	     1.9</p>
<p>Cathay Pacific     1.7	     1.8</p>
<p>Japan Airlines     1.7	     1.6</p>
<p>Air Outre Mer(AOM) 1.6	     n.a</p>
<p>United Airlines    1.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
